=09
		<span _msttexthash=3D"939653" _msthash=3D"1041">Future Applications of Me=
sh Systems</span>

=09
</span>		</h2>

			=09

<div class=3D"page-body se" id=3D"page5" data-slide=3D"5" data-track-gtm=3D=
"Content" x-show.transition=3D"pageVisible =3D=3D=3D true">=09



=09
		<p _msttexthash=3D"68187704" _msthash=3D"1042">The goals for mesh systems=
 extend beyond getting a reliable wi fi signal. The U.S. military, which <a=
 href=3D"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00502-006-0348-9" class=3D"ext-link">help=
ed develop wireless mesh technology</a>, foresees a day when thousands of m=
icrochip-size mesh nodes can be dropped onto a battlefield to set up instan=
t scouting and surveillance networks. Information can be routed to both gro=
und troops and headquartered personnel.</p>

	=09
=09
			=09
			=09
=09


=09
		<p _msttexthash=3D"60247356" _msthash=3D"1043">Carmakers and telecom comp=
anies are working to develop intelligent transport systems (ITS) using tech=
nologies including <a href=3D"http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-05029-4_1=
2" class=3D"ext-link">street and highway-based</a> wireless mesh networks. =
Using an automated network of surveillance cameras and in-car sensors, publ=
ic safety officials can tightly monitor traffic accidents and dangerous roa=
d conditions.</p>

	=09
=09
						=09

		<div class=3D"sticky-container ad-container print:hidden md:hidden h-min-=
400 mb-6" _msthidden=3D"1">
		<div class=3D"sticky top-99" _msthidden=3D"1">
	<p class=3D"ad-disclaimer clear-both text-xs text-center mb-1 md:hidden" _=
msttexthash=3D"235404" _msthidden=3D"1" _msthash=3D"1044">Advertisement</p>=
	<div id=3D"ad-wrap-mobinline11" class=3D"print:hidden md:hidden ad-inline =
ad-mobinline bg-gray w-max-full h-min-250"><div id=3D"ad-div-mobinline11" c=
lass=3D"ad-tag h-max-250"><div id=3D"mobinline__ayManagerEnv__233"></div><d=
iv id=3D"mobinline__ayManagerEnv__184"></div></div></div>		</div>
	</div>
=09
									=09
			=09
=09


=09
		<p _msttexthash=3D"107818672" _msthash=3D"1045">As they have become more =
common, wireless mesh networks have become valuable for powering internet o=
f things (IoT) devices with <a href=3D"https://dx.doi.org/10.3390%2Fs201542=
73" class=3D"ext-link">applications of all kinds</a>, including security, s=
mart agriculture, manufacturing, <a href=3D"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/doc=
ument/9139964" class=3D"ext-link">public utilities and environmental monito=
ring equipment</a>. Newer technologies, such as Bluetooth wireless mesh net=
works, also <a href=3D"https://www.bluetooth.com/blog/mesh-in-large-scale-n=
etworks/" class=3D"ext-link">support large IoT networks</a>. The future app=
lications for wireless mesh networks are limited only by our imaginations.<=
/p>

	=09
=09
			=09
			=09
=09

